        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e21" edge="1" parent="1" style="html=1;fontSize=11;endArrow=block;rounded=0;strokeColor=#333333;" value="9. Save the session in the browser">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="540" y="574" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="474" y="574" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e22" edge="1" parent="1" style="html=1;fontSize=11;endArrow=open;dashed=1;rounded=0;strokeColor=#666666;" value="10. Show the dashboard">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="470" y="604" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="180" y="604" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n23" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#ffffcc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;Points to explain&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Step 3 &amp;nbsp;After 10 failed attempts from one IP address in 15 minutes, the server stops responding to it.&lt;br&gt;Step 6 &amp;nbsp;Passwords are never stored or compared as plain text. Only the bcrypt hash is compared.&lt;br&gt;Step 7 &amp;nbsp;Both successful and failed logins are recorded, so there is a complete trail.&lt;br&gt;Step 8 &amp;nbsp;The token expires after 8 hours. The browser attaches it to every later request.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;If the password is wrong or the user does not exist&lt;/b&gt;, the server replies with exactly the same message,&lt;br&gt;&quot;Invalid username or password&quot;. This stops an attacker from discovering which usernames are real." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="170" width="900" x="80" y="700" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
